# EP-19 · Generated synthetic journey fixture. Regenerated by `npm run fixture:journey` (which
# `test:journey` always runs first), so it is never committed: a CSV of row-shaped data in the
# repository is exactly the thing that later gets mistaken for a real extract.
e2e/fixtures/*

# THE TWO FROZEN BENCHMARK PACKAGES ARE TRACKED EVIDENCE, and only their INPUTS.
#
# An uncommitted freeze is not a freeze. The V1 scorer's bytes "had never been committed", so the
# artefact had to be RECONSTRUCTED from recorded patches — and that it needed reconstructing is the
# compounding half of that disclosure. Three CI verifiers (`readiness:control`, `recon:verify`,
# `recon:ref:verify`) read these files, and `freeze.mjs` reads them with no existence guard, so on a
# clean checkout they would throw ENOENT and fail every run. Committing them is what lets CI verify the
# ARCHIVED bytes rather than bytes it just generated for itself.
#
# THE CAVEAT ABOVE STILL APPLIES AND IS ANSWERED RATHER THAN IGNORED: these are row-shaped CSVs, which
# is the thing that gets mistaken for a real extract. Every identifier in them is `syn-`/`SYN-`
# prefixed, there are no emails, no person names and no phone numbers, the directory names say
# synthetic, and each `FROZEN.json` records the generator hash and the seed. The journey fixture stays
# ignored because it is regenerated on every run and carries no freeze at all.
#
# RUN OUTPUTS STAY IGNORED. `results.json` alone is ~500 KB per package, it is rewritten by every
# `recon:run`/`recon:score`, and it is not evidence of the experiment's inputs — tracking it would make
# every run dirty the tree. The ten files below are 416 KB in total.
#
# THE FIFTEEN `baseline.*` ARTEFACTS ARE ALSO TRACKED, as of 2026-10-16, and they pass the inputs/outputs
# test on a checkable property rather than by argument: NO COMMAND WRITES ONE. `score.mjs` writes
# `scoreboard.json` and `report.txt`, `run.ts` writes `results.json`; a baseline is a copy taken BY HAND at
# a moment someone wanted to keep. That is what makes it a preserved historical measurement rather than a
# regenerated output, and it is why tracking one cannot dirty the tree on a routine run — the test
# `results.json` fails. Asserted by a test that scans every tracked script for a write whose target names
# a baseline. 327 KB in total.
#
# WHAT THEIR LEDGER ATTESTS, so it is stated where someone will look: continuity of these bytes from
# `e2e/evidence/reconciliation-baselines.evidence.json`'s `attestedAt` FORWARD. Not original provenance —
# no baseline file carries a core revision, a scorer revision or a timestamp, and none was ever tracked.
# Not historical reproducibility — the core has moved four times and a pre-correction baseline cannot run
# on this build at all. Not independent validation — one party produced, kept and attested all of it. Those
# three refusals are required literals in `src/evidence/baselineLedger.ts`, not prose.
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-synthetic/
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-obligation-ref/
e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-synthetic/*
e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-obligation-ref/*
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-*/expectation.csv
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-*/observation.csv
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-*/ground-truth.csv
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-*/planted-register.json
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-*/FROZEN.json
!e2e/fixtures/reconciliation-*/baseline.*

# THE TWO VALIDATION-CYCLE PACKAGES ARE TRACKED EVIDENCE, and only the artefacts their records HASH.
#
# `verify:evidence` re-hashes ten artefacts per cycle against a record committed to Git. Ten of those
# twenty — the five scripts in each `scripts/synthetic-validation*/` — were already tracked. The other ten
# were not, so on a clean checkout every one read `absent` and the verifier exited 1, which is why it could
# not be wired into CI. Proven by `git archive HEAD` before this rule existed: 10 absent failures.
#
# WHAT THEY ATTEST, stated here because the rule is where someone will look: CONTINUITY SINCE 2026-09-30,
# not original historical provenance. Neither cycle ever had a Git freeze, and `verify.mjs` overwrote the
# originally recorded gitHead/frozenAt, so both records carry `systemUnderTestRevision: "unknown"` and a
# downgrade marker. Tracking the bytes makes them verifiable from the date of the record forward. It does
# not make them older.
#
# SYNTHETIC BY CONSTRUCTION, checked rather than assumed: every identifier is `synthetic-`-prefixed and
# SEMANTIC — `synthetic-u-never-activated`, `synthetic-e-paid-exceeds` — naming the planted defect, which
# is the opposite of disguised real data. Zero emails, zero phone numbers, zero person names, zero free
# text. (The prefix is `synthetic-`, NOT the `syn-` of the reconciliation packages above: a scan looking
# for the wrong one reports zero identifiers on files where every row carries one.)
#
# EXACTLY THE HASH-COVERED ARTEFACTS, and nothing else. `raw-output.json` and `score.json` are run outputs;
# `*-v1`/`*-v2` are superseded generations; `FROZEN*.txt` likewise. `FROZEN.json` stays ignored on purpose —
# it is not hash-covered by the record (its substantive content, `runParameters`, is covered as a VALUE),
# so tracking it would put unverifiable bytes in the evidence set, and `attest:evidence` being unable to
# run from a clean checkout is correct: re-attesting is the act this scheme exists to make deliberate.
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation/
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation-2026-09-27/
e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation/*
e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation-2026-09-27/*
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation*/dataset.csv
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation*/spot-multicurrency.csv
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation*/spot-cancelled-after-asof.csv
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation*/ground-truth.json
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation*/prediction.json
#
# AND CYCLE 2'S RECORDED SCORE, added 2026-10-16 because the V2 diagnostic audit CITES IT. It is the only
# place the 2026-09-27 figures exist — $42,350.66 detectable, 27.27% class coverage, 34.64% value coverage
# — and the audit's comparison table quotes them, so leaving it untracked would make the report a receipt
# for a lost artefact. That is the governance decision the owner already made for `baseline.*`: a recorded
# historical MEASUREMENT is preserved evidence, not a disposable generated output. A recorded score is the
# same kind of object; it was simply outside the preservation slice's declared scope.
#
# It is NOT hash-covered by the evidence record, so `verify:evidence` does not check it and the report
# says so. Synthetic by construction: 44 KB, zero emails, every identifier `synthetic-`-prefixed.
# Cycle 1's score stays ignored — nothing cites it.
!e2e/fixtures/synthetic-validation-2026-09-27/score.json
